WEBVTT

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:13.034
The Barcelona Game by Stephen Rabbly Penguin Active Reading Level 1 Holly Hooper lives in Manchester.

00:00:13.094 --> 00:00:19.495
She has two brothers, Kev and Trev.

00:00:19.555 --> 00:00:26.627
Holly is twelve, quiet and loves books.

00:00:26.687 --> 00:00:34.448
The boys are seventeen, noisy and love football.

00:00:34.508 --> 00:00:40.270
One September morning, Kev runs into the kitchen.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:43.881
They're here, he shouts.

00:00:43.941 --> 00:00:48.512
The tickets for the Barcelona game are here.

00:00:48.572 --> 00:00:52.183
He dances across the kitchen floor.

00:00:52.243 --> 00:00:56.082
Holly is reading Oliver Twist.

00:00:56.142 --> 00:00:58.990
She puts her book down.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:01.613
The Barcelona game?

00:01:01.672 --> 00:01:03.364
She asks.

00:01:03.424 --> 00:01:05.666
What's that?

00:01:05.726 --> 00:01:09.388
Trevor looks at her.

00:01:09.448 --> 00:01:14.372
You don't know, he says.

00:01:14.432 --> 00:01:19.366
Manchester United are playing in Spain on Wednesday.

00:01:19.426 --> 00:01:22.528
Dad, Kevin, I are going.

00:01:22.587 --> 00:01:26.486
Oh, Holly says.

00:01:26.546 --> 00:01:31.594
But that evening, Dad isn't well.

00:01:31.654 --> 00:01:35.937
Next morning he talks to Kevin Trev.

00:01:35.996 --> 00:01:39.729
I'm sorry boys, he says.

00:01:39.789 --> 00:01:42.630
I've got a bad cold.

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:51.656
I can't go to a shoe to spend with you.

00:01:51.715 --> 00:01:57.128
But Dad, we've got three tickets for the aeroplane.

00:01:57.188 --> 00:02:01.219
Kev says, and three tickets for the game.

00:02:01.239 --> 00:02:07.002
And a hotel room for you too, Trev says.

00:02:07.062 --> 00:02:11.534
What are we going to do?

00:02:11.594 --> 00:02:15.686
The room is quiet.

00:02:15.746 --> 00:02:22.642
Then mum says, I know you can take Holly.

00:02:22.702 --> 00:02:26.186
Kev looks at Trev.

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:29.436
Trev looks at Kev.

00:02:29.496 --> 00:02:31.386
Yes!

00:02:31.446 --> 00:02:32.827
Dad says.

00:02:32.887 --> 00:02:34.697
That's the answer.

00:02:34.757 --> 00:02:39.858
It is the summer holidays, and she's doing Spanish at school too.

00:02:39.878 --> 00:02:42.908
But...

00:02:42.968 --> 00:02:45.399
Kev and Trev say.

00:02:45.459 --> 00:02:48.720
No buts, mum says.

00:02:48.779 --> 00:02:53.175
You're taking your little sister with you.

00:02:53.235 --> 00:02:57.661
The next day is Wednesday.

00:02:57.721 --> 00:03:02.302
Kev, Trev and Holly leave for Spain.

00:03:02.362 --> 00:03:05.363
Holly is very happy.

00:03:05.423 --> 00:03:10.254
On the airplane, she reads a book about Barcelona.

00:03:10.314 --> 00:03:14.696
There are a lot of photos in it.

00:03:14.755 --> 00:03:20.627
It's a beautiful place, she thinks.

00:03:20.687 --> 00:03:25.243
Behind her, the boys are sleeping.

00:03:25.303 --> 00:03:30.452
They arrive at Barcelona Airport at three o'clock.

00:03:30.511 --> 00:03:36.976
Okay, Trev says, let's take a taxi to the hotel.

00:03:37.036 --> 00:03:44.642
Then Holly says, oh no, and stops suddenly.

00:03:44.702 --> 00:03:48.366
She can see a big hole in her bag.

00:03:48.426 --> 00:03:52.356
Some of her books are falling on the floor.

00:03:52.415 --> 00:03:55.444
Kev looks at Trev.

00:03:55.504 --> 00:03:58.176
Trev looks at Kev.

00:03:58.236 --> 00:04:02.710
This is a good start, Kev says.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:06.693
Then he sees a small airport shop.

00:04:06.752 --> 00:04:09.684
There are some bags in the window.

00:04:09.744 --> 00:04:14.158
They have Barcelona on them.

00:04:14.218 --> 00:04:19.221
Go and buy a new bag, he tells Holly.

00:04:19.281 --> 00:04:22.798
But be quick, okay?

00:04:22.858 --> 00:04:26.766
Holly buys one of the Barcelona bags.

00:04:26.826 --> 00:04:32.150
Then she and her brothers take a taxi to their hotel.

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:35.232
Holly goes into her room.

00:04:35.292 --> 00:04:39.915
It has two windows and a very big bed.

00:04:39.975 --> 00:04:44.428
This is great, she thinks.

00:04:44.488 --> 00:04:48.832
Then she goes into Kev and Trev's room.

00:04:48.892 --> 00:04:50.556
Okay.

00:04:50.616 --> 00:04:53.159
What are we going to do before the game?

00:04:53.219 --> 00:04:54.810
She asks.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:05:08.834
We can see the Cathedral or the famous street Las Ramblas or the Olympic Stadium or no, no, no.

00:05:08.894 --> 00:05:10.394
Kev says.

00:05:10.454 --> 00:05:13.916
We don't want to go to those places.

00:05:13.976 --> 00:05:16.617
We're going to Tibidabo.

00:05:16.676 --> 00:05:19.594
It's a fun fair.

00:05:19.654 --> 00:05:23.532
Trev's friend went there in April.

00:05:23.592 --> 00:05:26.525
It's great, he says.

00:05:26.584 --> 00:05:30.377
A fun fair, Holly says.

00:05:30.437 --> 00:05:35.090
But no buts, Kev says.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:38.343
I'm telling you, it's great.

00:05:38.402 --> 00:05:43.175
We're going there and you're coming with us.

00:05:43.235 --> 00:05:49.439
Later, Holly and the boys arrive at Tibidabo.

00:05:49.498 --> 00:05:51.279
Look!

00:05:51.339 --> 00:05:53.470
There's a big wheel!

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:55.362
Trev says.

00:05:55.422 --> 00:05:58.656
I love big wheels.

00:05:58.715 --> 00:06:02.008
Me too, Kev says.

00:06:02.068 --> 00:06:03.370
Let's go!

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:07.914
Holly looks at the wheel.

00:06:07.974 --> 00:06:10.356
Oh, no!

00:06:10.415 --> 00:06:12.628
She thinks.

00:06:12.688 --> 00:06:19.129
Five minutes later, the wheel stops.

00:06:19.189 --> 00:06:24.838
That was great, Trev says.

00:06:24.898 --> 00:06:27.739
Let's do it again.

00:06:27.798 --> 00:06:30.420
Then he looks at Holly.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:33.712
Her face is white.

00:06:33.772 --> 00:06:36.072
Are you all right?

00:06:36.132 --> 00:06:37.874
He asks.

00:06:37.934 --> 00:06:39.614
No.

00:06:39.674 --> 00:06:41.584
Holly says.

00:06:41.644 --> 00:06:44.096
I'm not.

00:06:44.156 --> 00:06:47.187
Kev looks at Trev.

00:06:47.247 --> 00:06:50.290
Trev looks at Kev.

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:55.234
Okay, listen, Kev says.

00:06:55.294 --> 00:06:57.935
You see that cafe?

00:06:57.995 --> 00:07:00.436
Go and wait for us there.

00:07:00.496 --> 00:07:06.787
But stay there and don't move, okay?

00:07:06.847 --> 00:07:10.608
Okay, Holly says.

00:07:10.668 --> 00:07:15.270
And put the tickets in your bag, Kev says.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:18.703
We don't want to take them with us.

00:07:18.762 --> 00:07:22.056
See you at seven o'clock.

00:07:22.116 --> 00:07:23.766
Okay?

00:07:23.826 --> 00:07:25.677
Yes, Kev.

00:07:25.737 --> 00:07:27.508
Holly says.

00:07:27.568 --> 00:07:30.648
She puts the tickets in her bag.

00:07:30.708 --> 00:07:34.260
Then she walks to the cafe.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:40.022
At the cafe, Lamassia, Holly sits down.

00:07:40.082 --> 00:07:42.633
She asks for coffee.

00:07:42.693 --> 00:07:47.304
Then she looks at her Barcelona book.

00:07:47.364 --> 00:07:52.586
I wanted to see these places, she thinks.

00:07:52.646 --> 00:07:56.480
And now I'm not going to see them.

00:07:56.540 --> 00:08:02.925
I'm in Spain, and I'm only going to see a game of football.

00:08:02.985 --> 00:08:07.809
Her coffee comes, and she drinks it.

00:08:07.869 --> 00:08:14.665
Ten minutes later, a man sits at the next table.

00:08:14.725 --> 00:08:19.716
He has a moustache, and a brown coat.

00:08:19.776 --> 00:08:25.730
He has a bag with Barcelona on it.

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:31.504
Holly sees the bag and smiles.

00:08:31.564 --> 00:08:35.838
He's got one too, she thinks.

00:08:35.898 --> 00:08:38.449
Then she looks at her book again.

00:08:38.469 --> 00:08:48.215
The man drinks two black coffees and after that he leaves.

00:08:48.275 --> 00:08:53.298
Holly closes her book on Barcelona.

00:08:53.358 --> 00:08:57.180
Now what, she thinks?

00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:00.203
It's only six o'clock.

00:09:00.263 --> 00:09:07.078
Suddenly she remembers Oliver Twist and smiles.

00:09:07.138 --> 00:09:10.630
Her bag is on the floor.

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:17.596
Holly opens it, but then she stops smiling.

00:09:17.656 --> 00:09:33.839
blue shirt, an American newspaper, an address book with the name Fred Burns on it.

00:09:33.899 --> 00:09:38.262
These aren't my things, she thinks.

00:09:38.322 --> 00:09:41.414
I don't understand.

00:09:41.474 --> 00:09:44.076
Where's my book?

00:09:44.137 --> 00:09:51.017
Where are the tickets for the Then she closes her eyes.

00:09:51.077 --> 00:09:54.250
Oh no!

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:57.682
The man with the moustache.

00:09:57.742 --> 00:10:01.074
This isn't my bag.

00:10:01.134 --> 00:10:03.936
It's his.

00:10:03.996 --> 00:10:07.058
She stands up.

00:10:07.118 --> 00:10:11.340
Suddenly her hands are cold.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:12.822
Where is he?

00:10:12.882 --> 00:10:15.362
Where is he?

00:10:15.422 --> 00:10:20.094
She runs out of the cafe.

00:10:20.154 --> 00:10:23.606
There are a lot of people in the street.

00:10:23.666 --> 00:10:28.307
Holly looks left and right.

00:10:28.367 --> 00:10:34.839
I can't see him, she thinks.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:39.922
A boy on a motorbike is passing the cafe.

00:10:39.982 --> 00:10:44.048
He sees Holly's face and stops.

00:10:44.108 --> 00:10:46.194
What's wrong?

00:10:46.254 --> 00:10:48.474
He asks her.

00:10:48.534 --> 00:10:51.646
She starts to tell him.

00:10:51.706 --> 00:10:55.768
Then she looks across the street.

00:10:55.828 --> 00:10:59.298
A taxi is driving away.

00:10:59.358 --> 00:11:03.720
Fred Burns is sitting in the back.

00:11:03.781 --> 00:11:07.242
That's him, she shouts.

00:11:07.302 --> 00:11:09.233
There he goes.

00:11:09.292 --> 00:11:12.204
He's got my bag.

00:11:12.264 --> 00:11:14.170
Stop!

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:17.059
Stop!

00:11:17.119 --> 00:11:21.472
He can't hear you, says the boy.

00:11:21.532 --> 00:11:24.785
The traffic's very noisy.

00:11:24.845 --> 00:11:26.476
Listen!

00:11:26.536 --> 00:11:30.570
Do you want to follow him?

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:34.993
Holly looks at the boy.

00:11:35.053 --> 00:11:37.004
How?

00:11:37.064 --> 00:11:39.937
On your motorbike?

00:11:39.997 --> 00:11:42.414
Yes.

00:11:42.474 --> 00:11:46.020
Holly thinks about it.

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:50.492
Okay, she says.

00:11:50.552 --> 00:11:54.524
The boy gives her a crash helmet.

00:11:54.584 --> 00:11:58.286
Put this on, he says.

00:11:58.346 --> 00:12:03.598
Holly sits behind him and puts it on.

00:12:03.658 --> 00:12:06.368
What's your name?

00:12:06.428 --> 00:12:08.389
She asks.

00:12:08.449 --> 00:12:12.444
Peré, the boy answers.

00:12:12.504 --> 00:12:18.561
Then he starts the bike and drives quickly away.

00:12:18.621 --> 00:12:22.934
Holly closes her eyes.

00:12:22.994 --> 00:12:29.618
Fred burns his taxi, is yellow and black.

00:12:29.678 --> 00:12:37.582
It goes left, right and left again very quickly.

00:12:37.642 --> 00:12:40.504
Peri follows it.

00:12:40.564 --> 00:12:43.936
Holly opens her eyes.

00:12:43.996 --> 00:12:47.750
They are passing a big building.

00:12:47.810 --> 00:12:52.553
She remembers one of the photos in her book.

00:12:52.613 --> 00:12:58.278
That's the Olympic stadium, she thinks.

00:12:58.338 --> 00:13:07.204
Ten minutes later, Fred Burns' taxi is in the famous street, Las Ramblas.

00:13:07.264 --> 00:13:11.538
Holly can see her bag in the back window.

00:13:11.598 --> 00:13:15.218
She can see Fred Burns too.

00:13:15.278 --> 00:13:19.676
Please stop, she thinks.

00:13:19.736 --> 00:13:22.996
Where are you going?

00:13:23.056 --> 00:13:27.048
There are some traffic lights in front of them.

00:13:27.108 --> 00:13:31.738
They go from green to yellow.

00:13:31.798 --> 00:13:39.771
The taxi passes the lights, but then the lights go red.

00:13:39.831 --> 00:13:45.429
Two old women start to walk across the street.

00:13:45.489 --> 00:13:50.218
They have got a lot of flowers in their hands.

00:13:50.278 --> 00:13:52.909
Oh, no!

00:13:52.969 --> 00:13:54.870
Holly says.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:59.042
She looks at the back of Fred Burns' head.

00:13:59.102 --> 00:14:02.614
We can't catch him now.

00:14:02.674 --> 00:14:04.815
Yes, we can!

00:14:04.835 --> 00:14:07.476
Perry shouts.

00:14:07.536 --> 00:14:12.558
He drives in front of the two women very quickly.

00:14:12.618 --> 00:14:16.061
One says, aye!

00:14:16.121 --> 00:14:23.064
Sorry, Perry shouts and drives away.

00:14:23.124 --> 00:14:27.986
Perry follows the taxi for a long time.

00:14:28.046 --> 00:14:33.999
Then it stops near Barcelona's famous cathedral.

00:14:34.059 --> 00:14:38.651
Holly and Perry stop too.

00:14:38.711 --> 00:14:43.918
There are a lot of people and cars in front of the cathedral.

00:14:43.978 --> 00:14:49.148
It's a beautiful building, Holly thinks.

00:14:49.208 --> 00:14:53.090
Then she remembers Fred Burns.

00:14:53.150 --> 00:14:58.434
Look, there he is, Perry says.

00:14:58.494 --> 00:15:01.978
He's getting out of the taxi.

00:15:02.038 --> 00:15:05.960
Holly takes off her crash helmet.

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:09.354
Stop, she shouts.

00:15:09.414 --> 00:15:13.603
Mr. Burns, please stop.

00:15:13.664 --> 00:15:18.974
She gets off the bike and starts to run.

00:15:19.034 --> 00:15:23.026
Peré watches the English girl.

00:15:23.086 --> 00:15:26.438
She is running very quickly.

00:15:26.498 --> 00:15:31.300
Fred Burns is walking into the cathedral.

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:37.763
The American hears his name and stops.

00:15:37.823 --> 00:15:42.224
Me, he says.

00:15:42.284 --> 00:15:45.374
He looks left and right.

00:15:45.434 --> 00:15:48.096
Then he sees Holly.

00:15:48.156 --> 00:15:52.730
She runs to him and starts talking.

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:57.674
Two minutes later, she comes back to Perry.

00:15:57.734 --> 00:16:01.336
There is a big smile on her face.

00:16:01.396 --> 00:16:04.950
Have you got the right bag now?

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:06.650
He asks.

00:16:06.710 --> 00:16:09.934
Yes, I have.

00:16:09.994 --> 00:16:12.983
Holly is very happy.

00:16:13.044 --> 00:16:16.953
Oh, Perry, thank you.

00:16:17.013 --> 00:16:19.304
How can I?

00:16:19.364 --> 00:16:23.506
But then she stops smiling.

00:16:23.566 --> 00:16:25.946
Oh, no!

00:16:26.006 --> 00:16:28.368
What time is it?

00:16:28.428 --> 00:16:31.438
Perry looks at his watch.

00:16:31.498 --> 00:16:33.619
Twenty to seven.

00:16:33.679 --> 00:16:36.570
Why?

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:42.710
Suddenly, Holly's face is white again.

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:50.469
They're going to be at Lamassia in 20 minutes.

00:16:50.529 --> 00:16:56.630
She tells Perry about her brothers and the football game.

00:16:56.690 --> 00:17:01.491
I understand, the Spanish boy says.

00:17:01.551 --> 00:17:06.342
Okay, put your helmet on again.

00:17:06.402 --> 00:17:12.300
Perry and Holly drive back to Lamassia very quickly.

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:16.638
They pass a lot of beautiful old buildings.

00:17:16.698 --> 00:17:20.931
This is great, Holly thinks.

00:17:20.992 --> 00:17:25.054
I'm seeing Barcelona now.

00:17:25.115 --> 00:17:32.870
Five minutes later, she and Peré pass the big wheel at Tibidabo.

00:17:32.930 --> 00:17:35.522
What time is it now?

00:17:35.582 --> 00:17:38.494
Holly asks.

00:17:38.554 --> 00:17:44.407
One minute to seven, the Spanish boy says.

00:17:44.467 --> 00:17:46.298
It's okay.

00:17:46.358 --> 00:17:49.330
You're not going to be late.

00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:53.022
He stops in front of the cafe.

00:17:53.082 --> 00:17:56.334
Holly looks at the people there.

00:17:56.394 --> 00:17:59.276
Good, she says.

00:17:59.336 --> 00:18:02.429
Kevin Trev aren't here.

00:18:02.489 --> 00:18:06.254
Then she gets off the motorbike.

00:18:06.315 --> 00:18:10.069
Peré, how can I thank you?"

00:18:10.129 --> 00:18:11.950
she says.

00:18:12.010 --> 00:18:14.480
That's okay.

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:16.351
Peré answers.

00:18:16.411 --> 00:18:19.542
I had a good time.

00:18:19.602 --> 00:18:22.883
He looks at his motorbike.

00:18:22.943 --> 00:18:26.764
There are two red flowers in one of the wheels.

00:18:26.824 --> 00:18:32.912
Here, he says, and he gives the flowers to Holly.

00:18:32.972 --> 00:18:36.490
These flowers are for you.

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:39.381
Have a good time at the game.

00:18:39.441 --> 00:18:42.252
Okay?

00:18:42.312 --> 00:18:47.084
He smiles and starts his bike.

00:18:47.144 --> 00:18:50.926
Then he drives away.

00:18:50.986 --> 00:18:55.488
Kevin Trev arrive at the cafe.

00:18:55.548 --> 00:18:59.550
Holly is reading Oliver Twist.

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:01.950
She looks up.

00:19:02.010 --> 00:19:05.171
Oh hello, she says.

00:19:05.231 --> 00:19:08.404
Are we going now?

00:19:08.464 --> 00:19:14.368
There are a lot of people in the new camp football stadium.

00:19:14.428 --> 00:19:20.244
Kev, Trev and Holly get there ten minutes before the game.

00:19:20.304 --> 00:19:22.906
Have you got the tickets?

00:19:22.966 --> 00:19:25.288
Kev asks his sister.

00:19:25.348 --> 00:19:31.578
Yes, Holly says, and she takes them from her bag.

00:19:31.638 --> 00:19:35.438
The boys buy food and drinks.

00:19:35.498 --> 00:19:40.151
Then they all sit down.

00:19:40.211 --> 00:19:45.826
We had a great time this afternoon.

00:19:45.886 --> 00:19:47.736
Trev says.

00:19:47.797 --> 00:19:50.850
Yes, Kev says.

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:53.691
A great time.

00:19:53.751 --> 00:19:57.014
Good, Holly says.

00:19:57.074 --> 00:19:59.466
Me too.

00:19:59.526 --> 00:20:02.788
Kev looks at Trev.

00:20:02.848 --> 00:20:05.858
Trev looks at Kev.

00:20:05.918 --> 00:20:12.390
Then they look at their little sister and smile.

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:14.740
You, Kev says.

00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:18.712
Holly, you never have.

00:20:18.772 --> 00:20:22.772
But the players are coming into the stadium.

00:20:22.832 --> 00:20:24.873
United!

00:20:24.933 --> 00:20:26.664
United!

00:20:26.724 --> 00:20:29.221
Kev and Trev shout.

00:20:29.281 --> 00:20:32.140
Holly looks at them.

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:37.074
Yes, me, she thinks.

00:20:37.134 --> 00:20:40.428
